==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|desjoindre}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪsˈdʒɔɪnt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɔɪnt|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# not smooth or [[continuous]]; [[disjointed]]
# {{lb|en|set theory}} (''not used in the comparative or superlative'') Of two or more [[set]]s, having no members in common; having an [[intersection]] equal to the [[empty set]].

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|non-disjoint}}
* {{l|en|overlapping}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|disjunct}}
* {{l|en|conjoint}}

